1
00:00:03,433 --> 00:00:05,300
I'm Peppa Pig. [snorts]

2
00:00:05,366 --> 00:00:08,033
-This is my little brother, George.
-[snorts]

3
00:00:08,100 --> 00:00:10,333
-This is Mommy Pig.
-[Mommy Pig snorts]

4
00:00:10,400 --> 00:00:11,799
And this is Daddy Pig.

5
00:00:12,033 --> 00:00:14,133
-[Daddy Pig snorts]
-[all laugh]

6
00:00:14,200 --> 00:00:15,766
Peppa Pig. [snorts]

7
00:00:17,800 --> 00:00:19,500
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

8
00:00:20,533 --> 00:00:22,733
[narrator] It is home time
at Peppa's playgroup.

9
00:00:22,800 --> 00:00:26,299
[snorts] Daddy, Teddy Playgroup
is coming to stay.

10
00:00:26,366 --> 00:00:29,466
-Who?
-Teddy Playgroup is our school mascot.

11
00:00:29,533 --> 00:00:31,766
It's Peppa's turn to take him home.

12
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:36,600
He has pajamas, a photo album
and a toothbrush.

13
00:00:36,666 --> 00:00:39,133
It's all in his suitcase.

14
00:00:39,199 --> 00:00:40,133
I see.

15
00:00:41,666 --> 00:00:42,533
[horn honks]

16
00:00:42,600 --> 00:00:46,433
[narrator] Peppa, Daddy Pig
and Teddy Playgroup have arrived home.

17
00:00:47,066 --> 00:00:50,766
Mommy Pig, we have a special guest
staying with us tonight.

18
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:52,433
Really? Who's that?

19
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:54,199
Teddy Playgroup.

20
00:00:54,266 --> 00:00:59,333
He has pajamas, a photo album
and a toothbrush.

21
00:00:59,400 --> 00:01:01,266
What is the photo album for?

22
00:01:01,333 --> 00:01:05,700
We take photos of him
doing exciting things.

23
00:01:05,766 --> 00:01:06,633
Oh.

24
00:01:06,700 --> 00:01:10,700
My friends have took Teddy Playgroup
all over the world.

25
00:01:11,533 --> 00:01:15,233
[Mommy Pig] London, Paris, Egypt...

26
00:01:15,300 --> 00:01:18,566
Oh, I say, Teddy Playgroup
does have an exciting life.

27
00:01:18,633 --> 00:01:21,800
Um, I hope he has an exciting time
with us.

28
00:01:24,166 --> 00:01:26,166
[narrator] It is Peppa
and George's bedtime.

29
00:01:26,233 --> 00:01:27,633
[Peppa &amp; George giggling]

30
00:01:27,700 --> 00:01:31,100
Everybody, this is Teddy Playgroup.

31
00:01:31,166 --> 00:01:32,166
[in deep voice] Hello.

32
00:01:32,233 --> 00:01:34,233
[in normal voice] He is our special guest.

33
00:01:34,300 --> 00:01:36,333
You all have to make room.

34
00:01:37,600 --> 00:01:38,766
Grr.

35
00:01:39,000 --> 00:01:42,100
Oh. And that is Mr. Dinosaur.

36
00:01:42,166 --> 00:01:44,533
He's not very good at talking.

37
00:01:44,600 --> 00:01:45,699
Grr.

38
00:01:45,766 --> 00:01:47,466
[Peppa &amp; George giggle]

39
00:01:47,533 --> 00:01:50,233
Let's take a photo
for Teddy Playgroup's album.

40
00:01:50,300 --> 00:01:52,699
[snorts] Say cheese.

41
00:01:52,766 --> 00:01:54,066
Cheese.

42
00:01:54,500 --> 00:02:00,433
Daddy, Teddy Playgroup needs
to have an exciting time tomorrow.

43
00:02:00,500 --> 00:02:02,666
Can we go to the North Pole?

44
00:02:02,733 --> 00:02:05,300
Uh... how about the supermarket?

45
00:02:05,366 --> 00:02:06,566
Yes! [snorts]

46
00:02:06,633 --> 00:02:11,000
I don't think Teddy Playgroup
has ever been shopping before.

47
00:02:11,733 --> 00:02:13,566
-[horn honks]
-[narrator] It is morning.

48
00:02:13,633 --> 00:02:16,666
Peppa is taking Teddy Playgroup
to the supermarket.

49
00:02:16,733 --> 00:02:17,666
[Peppa giggles]

50
00:02:17,733 --> 00:02:20,066
This shop sells everything.

51
00:02:20,533 --> 00:02:23,500
Oranges, apples, bananas.

52
00:02:24,000 --> 00:02:26,666
[in deep voice] Very interesting.

53
00:02:26,733 --> 00:02:28,400
[giggles]

54
00:02:28,466 --> 00:02:31,666
[narrator] This is the checkout
where all the food is paid for.

55
00:02:31,733 --> 00:02:33,066
[George giggles]

56
00:02:33,133 --> 00:02:35,233
[narrator] George wants to take a picture.

57
00:02:35,299 --> 00:02:37,666
-Okay, George.
-[snorts] Cheese.

58
00:02:37,733 --> 00:02:39,066
[both] Cheese.

59
00:02:41,466 --> 00:02:44,466
[laughs] That's enough pictures, George.

60
00:02:44,533 --> 00:02:45,666
[George giggles]

61
00:02:48,566 --> 00:02:51,200
Oh! Where is Teddy Playgroup?

62
00:02:51,266 --> 00:02:53,100
[narrator] Teddy Playgroup is missing.

63
00:02:53,166 --> 00:02:56,500
Daddy, you've lost Teddy Playgroup.

64
00:02:56,566 --> 00:02:58,000
Don't worry, Peppa.

65
00:02:58,066 --> 00:02:59,766
I'm sure we'll find him.

66
00:03:01,233 --> 00:03:02,433
Hello. [snorts]

67
00:03:02,500 --> 00:03:03,666
How was your day?

68
00:03:03,733 --> 00:03:06,166
Daddy lost Teddy Playgroup.

69
00:03:06,233 --> 00:03:07,200
Oh, no.

70
00:03:07,266 --> 00:03:09,566
But I've got a plan to find him.

71
00:03:11,166 --> 00:03:14,299
How are we going
to find Teddy Playgroup, Daddy?

72
00:03:14,366 --> 00:03:18,166
First, we print out all the photos
we took of him.

73
00:03:24,066 --> 00:03:26,233
[narrator] Mommy Pig
is unpacking the shopping.

74
00:03:26,299 --> 00:03:27,466
Where are you going?

75
00:03:27,533 --> 00:03:30,766
We're going to stick pictures
of Teddy Playgroup on trees.

76
00:03:31,000 --> 00:03:32,100
Oh.

77
00:03:33,200 --> 00:03:34,799
Daddy, wait for me.

78
00:03:35,633 --> 00:03:38,266
Why are we sticking photos
on trees, Daddy?

79
00:03:38,333 --> 00:03:41,633
[snorts] When people see the pictures
of Teddy Playgroup,

80
00:03:41,700 --> 00:03:44,733
they'll know he's lost,
and they can help us find him.

81
00:03:44,799 --> 00:03:46,133
[Peppa] Oh.

82
00:03:46,200 --> 00:03:48,033
This is Teddy in my bed.

83
00:03:48,600 --> 00:03:50,100
[Peppa giggles]

84
00:03:50,166 --> 00:03:53,533
This is Teddy in the kitchen. [giggles]

85
00:03:54,166 --> 00:03:58,399
And these are George's pictures
at the supermarket.

86
00:03:58,466 --> 00:04:00,633
Oh! Teddy Playgroup. [snorts]

87
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:02,600
I know where he is.

88
00:04:02,666 --> 00:04:04,566
[Peppa &amp; George giggle]

89
00:04:05,200 --> 00:04:06,333
Oh, hello.

90
00:04:06,766 --> 00:04:10,166
Mommy, we know where Teddy Playgroup is.

91
00:04:10,233 --> 00:04:13,666
Yes. He's in the shopping bag
with the pasta and tomatoes.

92
00:04:13,733 --> 00:04:15,500
[all laughing]

93
00:04:15,566 --> 00:04:17,166
[bell rings]

94
00:04:17,233 --> 00:04:20,800
[narrator] Peppa is showing her class
Teddy Playgroup's photo album.

95
00:04:21,033 --> 00:04:22,500
I was worried

96
00:04:22,566 --> 00:04:27,033
that Teddy Playgroup wouldn't
have an exciting adventure with us.

97
00:04:27,099 --> 00:04:32,766
Then, luckily, my Daddy lost him
at the supermarket.

98
00:04:33,000 --> 00:04:36,599
-[students gasp]
-But we found him again in the shopping.

99
00:04:36,666 --> 00:04:38,000
[students] Ooh.

100
00:04:38,066 --> 00:04:40,300
That was an exciting adventure.

101
00:04:40,366 --> 00:04:42,133
[in deep voice] Yes, it was.

102
00:04:42,200 --> 00:04:44,200
[all laughing]

103
00:04:49,533 --> 00:04:52,200
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

104
00:04:52,266 --> 00:04:55,800
[narrator] Today is Danny Dog's birthday.
He is having a party.

105
00:04:56,033 --> 00:04:58,433
[woofs] Yo-ho-ho!

106
00:04:58,500 --> 00:05:00,700
[narrator] Everyone has come dressed
as pirates.

107
00:05:00,766 --> 00:05:02,366
[children] Yo-ho-ho!

108
00:05:02,433 --> 00:05:04,800
[narrator] Pedro Pony is dressed
as a cowboy.

109
00:05:05,033 --> 00:05:06,233
Yeehaw!

110
00:05:06,300 --> 00:05:07,266
[children giggle]

111
00:05:07,333 --> 00:05:10,200
[woofs] Ahoy there, me hearties.

112
00:05:10,266 --> 00:05:13,300
[narrator] It is Granddad Dog,
dressed as a pirate.

113
00:05:13,366 --> 00:05:15,500
[snorts] Hello, Granddad Dog.

114
00:05:15,566 --> 00:05:17,733
Call me Dog Beard.

115
00:05:17,800 --> 00:05:19,733
[children] Hello, Dog Beard.

116
00:05:19,800 --> 00:05:23,666
[woofs] Which of ye scurvy pirates
crave a ration

117
00:05:23,733 --> 00:05:26,133
of swashbuckling o'er the briny seas?

118
00:05:26,200 --> 00:05:27,700
Why is he talking funny?

119
00:05:27,766 --> 00:05:30,333
[giggles] That's pirate's talk.

120
00:05:30,400 --> 00:05:35,099
If you want to play my pirate game,
say "arr."

121
00:05:35,166 --> 00:05:36,400
[children] Arr!

122
00:05:36,466 --> 00:05:40,066
-Is it a dangerous game?
-No, Pedro.

123
00:05:40,133 --> 00:05:44,766
Granddad Dog has promised me
it will be a very safe game.

124
00:05:45,000 --> 00:05:46,033
[children] Aw.

125
00:05:46,099 --> 00:05:48,133
But it will be exciting.

126
00:05:48,200 --> 00:05:50,700
-So, who wants to play?
-[children] Arr!

127
00:05:50,766 --> 00:05:52,366
Here be the plan.

128
00:05:53,033 --> 00:05:56,200
Time was, I had a heap of gold
that was mine by right.

129
00:05:56,266 --> 00:05:59,266
But I was hornswoggled by one Captain Hog.

130
00:06:00,266 --> 00:06:01,266
What?

131
00:06:01,333 --> 00:06:04,500
[narrator] Pirate talk is a bit difficult
to understand.

132
00:06:04,566 --> 00:06:07,733
Captain Hog took my treasure.

133
00:06:07,800 --> 00:06:09,300
[children] Ohh.

134
00:06:09,366 --> 00:06:14,533
Know you
that Captain Hog is a fearsome pirate.

135
00:06:14,599 --> 00:06:20,299
Some of you may already know him
as Grandpa Pig.

136
00:06:20,366 --> 00:06:22,799
[children] Ah. Grandpa Pig.

137
00:06:23,033 --> 00:06:24,066
[all giggle]

138
00:06:24,133 --> 00:06:28,633
The game is to go to Captain Hog's hideout
and get back my treasure

139
00:06:28,700 --> 00:06:30,166
without being caught.

140
00:06:30,233 --> 00:06:31,533
[all] Hooray!

141
00:06:31,599 --> 00:06:34,700
[narrator] Everyone is excited
to be playing the pirate game.

142
00:06:34,766 --> 00:06:36,000
[dialing]

143
00:06:36,066 --> 00:06:36,766
[line rings]

144
00:06:37,000 --> 00:06:38,266
Hello, Grandpa Pig.

145
00:06:38,333 --> 00:06:39,433
We're on our way.

146
00:06:40,066 --> 00:06:40,766
Jolly good.

147
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:41,799
Jolly good.

148
00:06:42,433 --> 00:06:46,433
[narrator] Grandpa Pig and Polly Parrot
are guarding the pirate treasure.

149
00:06:47,066 --> 00:06:51,366
Be the Black Galleon fast
and the wind at our backs we'll away.

150
00:06:51,433 --> 00:06:53,200
What does that mean?

151
00:06:53,266 --> 00:06:54,566
Run to the boat.

152
00:06:54,633 --> 00:06:56,233
[children] Yo-ho-ho!

153
00:06:56,299 --> 00:06:57,599
Yeehaw!

154
00:06:57,666 --> 00:06:58,566
[children giggle]

155
00:07:00,500 --> 00:07:01,433
Whoa, there.

156
00:07:01,500 --> 00:07:03,233
Put your life jackets on.

157
00:07:03,700 --> 00:07:07,733
[narrator] On Granddad Dog's boat,
all the children must wear life jackets.

158
00:07:08,733 --> 00:07:13,566
That scurvy Dog Beard should
be here by now. [snorts]

159
00:07:13,633 --> 00:07:16,133
Here's a nice cup of tea, Grandpa Pig.

160
00:07:16,200 --> 00:07:18,533
Oh, thank you, Granny Pig.

161
00:07:20,099 --> 00:07:21,200
At last.

162
00:07:21,266 --> 00:07:23,000
Are we all ready now?

163
00:07:23,066 --> 00:07:27,366
Mr. Dog Beard, I need to go to the toilet.

164
00:07:27,433 --> 00:07:29,266
-And me.
-And me.

165
00:07:29,333 --> 00:07:31,000
-And me.
-And me.

166
00:07:31,066 --> 00:07:31,766
And me.

167
00:07:32,400 --> 00:07:34,599
What can be keeping them?

168
00:07:34,666 --> 00:07:36,299
[dialing]

169
00:07:36,366 --> 00:07:38,700
Hello, Granddad Dog?

170
00:07:38,766 --> 00:07:41,466
I thought you said you were on your way.

171
00:07:41,533 --> 00:07:44,066
Yes, yes, we're almost there.

172
00:07:44,133 --> 00:07:46,666
It's taken a while
to get my crew together.

173
00:07:47,333 --> 00:07:49,133
Anchors away.

174
00:07:49,200 --> 00:07:50,566
Full sail.

175
00:07:50,633 --> 00:07:52,599
[children] Aye, aye, Dog Beard.

176
00:07:52,666 --> 00:07:54,133
[children giggles]

177
00:07:54,200 --> 00:07:56,299
♪ Oh, jolly pirates, we ♪

178
00:07:56,366 --> 00:07:58,333
♪ That sail the deep blue sea ♪

179
00:07:58,400 --> 00:08:00,433
♪ To find our golden treasure ♪

180
00:08:00,500 --> 00:08:02,766
♪ Full sail, ahoy, yippee! ♪

181
00:08:03,000 --> 00:08:04,400
Land ahoy.

182
00:08:05,466 --> 00:08:08,633
[narrator] The children have arrived
at Grandpa Pig's orchard.

183
00:08:08,700 --> 00:08:09,599
[children giggle]

184
00:08:09,666 --> 00:08:15,066
The game is to get that treasure
without being caught.

185
00:08:16,200 --> 00:08:18,066
[mothers] Hooray for the pirates.

186
00:08:18,133 --> 00:08:19,299
Shush, Mommy.

187
00:08:21,566 --> 00:08:25,500
I hope there are no pirates around here,

188
00:08:25,566 --> 00:08:29,099
trying to take my lovely treasure.

189
00:08:29,166 --> 00:08:33,066
[narrator] Peppa and her friends
have got the coins without being caught.

190
00:08:33,133 --> 00:08:35,666
It's chocolate coins.

191
00:08:35,733 --> 00:08:38,233
[narrator] Everybody loves
chocolate coins.

192
00:08:38,299 --> 00:08:40,066
[all] Yum, yum, yum.

193
00:08:40,666 --> 00:08:42,100
Ah.

194
00:08:42,166 --> 00:08:44,666
-Got you.
-[narrator] Granddad Dog has been caught.

195
00:08:44,733 --> 00:08:47,500
Try and take my treasure, would you?

196
00:08:47,566 --> 00:08:48,566
'Tis mine.

197
00:08:48,633 --> 00:08:50,633
I won it fair and square.

198
00:08:50,699 --> 00:08:52,666
Oh, no, you didn't.

199
00:08:52,733 --> 00:08:54,666
Oh, yes, I did.

200
00:08:54,733 --> 00:08:56,400
[barking and snorting]

201
00:08:56,466 --> 00:08:59,699
[clears throat] Thank you,
Captain Hog and Dog Beard,

202
00:08:59,766 --> 00:09:04,166
-for the lovely pirate game.
-Oh, you're very welcome.

203
00:09:04,233 --> 00:09:05,466
Uh, oh, yes.

204
00:09:05,533 --> 00:09:07,500
It's been lots of fun.

205
00:09:07,566 --> 00:09:10,100
[children] Happy Birthday, Danny.

206
00:09:10,166 --> 00:09:13,300
This be the best pirate party ever!

207
00:09:13,366 --> 00:09:14,766
[all] Arr!

208
00:09:15,000 --> 00:09:16,766
[all laughing]

209
00:09:19,166 --> 00:09:21,166
[Peppa reading on-screen text]

210
00:09:22,266 --> 00:09:23,766
[Mr. Potato] Up, down, up, down...

211
00:09:24,000 --> 00:09:27,500
[narrator] Peppa and her family
are watching Mr. Potato on television.

212
00:09:28,066 --> 00:09:31,366
[snorts] I love watching programs
about keeping fit.

213
00:09:31,433 --> 00:09:32,400
Up, down.

214
00:09:32,466 --> 00:09:36,766
Now, here are some lovely drawings
I've been sent.

215
00:09:37,000 --> 00:09:38,566
This is an apple.

216
00:09:38,633 --> 00:09:39,666
[Peppa &amp; George] Ooh.

217
00:09:39,733 --> 00:09:45,100
Remember, eating fruit
and vegetables helps you stay fit.

218
00:09:45,166 --> 00:09:48,199
I'm good at eating fruits and vegetables.

219
00:09:48,266 --> 00:09:50,766
And exercise is important.

220
00:09:51,000 --> 00:09:55,133
Today you can see me open
a new sports center in town.

221
00:09:56,699 --> 00:10:00,166
Mommy, can we go and see Mr. Potato?

222
00:10:00,233 --> 00:10:03,066
It's a long way to go
to see a potato, Peppa.

223
00:10:03,133 --> 00:10:04,633
He's not any old potato.

224
00:10:04,699 --> 00:10:07,400
[snorts] This is Mr. Potato.

225
00:10:07,466 --> 00:10:11,166
Can we go and see him, Mommy, please?

226
00:10:11,233 --> 00:10:13,533
-Oh, all right.
-[Daddy Pig &amp; children] Hooray!

227
00:10:13,600 --> 00:10:14,666
[all laugh]

228
00:10:16,433 --> 00:10:20,566
[narrator] Everyone has come to see
Mr. Potato open the new sports center.

229
00:10:20,633 --> 00:10:22,133
[horn honking]

230
00:10:22,199 --> 00:10:24,500
Look. It's Mr. Potato.

231
00:10:24,566 --> 00:10:26,600
[crowd] Mr. Potato!

232
00:10:26,666 --> 00:10:29,433
-[horn honks]
-Oh, it's just Peppa.

233
00:10:29,500 --> 00:10:30,366
[crowd] Oh.

234
00:10:30,433 --> 00:10:32,000
Hello, everyone.

235
00:10:32,066 --> 00:10:33,333
[crowd] Hello, Peppa.

236
00:10:33,400 --> 00:10:36,333
Suzy thought you were Mr. Potato.

237
00:10:36,400 --> 00:10:39,666
[snorts] I don't look like Mr. Potato.

238
00:10:39,733 --> 00:10:42,000
No, you're much too big.

239
00:10:42,066 --> 00:10:45,233
Mr. Potato is bigger than me.

240
00:10:45,300 --> 00:10:46,433
No, he's not.

241
00:10:46,500 --> 00:10:48,033
He's a potato.

242
00:10:48,100 --> 00:10:50,199
And potatoes are this big.

243
00:10:50,266 --> 00:10:51,133
[horn honking]

244
00:10:51,199 --> 00:10:53,166
[woofs] There's Mr. Potato.

245
00:10:55,033 --> 00:10:57,666
[narrator] Mr. Potato has come to town.

246
00:10:58,466 --> 00:11:04,133
Please, welcome your friend
and mine, Mr. Potato.

247
00:11:04,199 --> 00:11:05,800
[crowd] Hooray!

248
00:11:06,033 --> 00:11:08,600
Wow, that's a big potato.

249
00:11:09,166 --> 00:11:12,400
I declare this sports center open.

250
00:11:15,199 --> 00:11:16,333
Fantastic.

251
00:11:16,400 --> 00:11:21,333
We must all exercise
and eat fruit and vegetables.

252
00:11:21,400 --> 00:11:24,333
Which ones should we eat, Mr. Potato?

253
00:11:24,400 --> 00:11:28,400
Apples, oranges, carrots, tomatoes.

254
00:11:28,466 --> 00:11:30,500
-Potatoes?
-Um...

255
00:11:30,566 --> 00:11:34,266
Why aren't you small,
like a normal potato?

256
00:11:34,333 --> 00:11:37,733
-Uh...
-Because he's not a normal potato.

257
00:11:38,366 --> 00:11:40,000
He's got legs.

258
00:11:40,066 --> 00:11:43,100
Normal potatoes don't have legs.

259
00:11:43,166 --> 00:11:45,133
He's a super potato.

260
00:11:45,199 --> 00:11:48,466
[snorts] We watch your show every morning.

261
00:11:48,533 --> 00:11:50,033
Very good.

262
00:11:50,100 --> 00:11:52,500
And remember to send me your drawings.

263
00:11:52,566 --> 00:11:53,733
[children] We will.

264
00:11:53,800 --> 00:11:54,800
[children giggle]

265
00:11:55,033 --> 00:11:55,800
[bell rings]

266
00:11:56,033 --> 00:11:58,400
[narrator] Peppa and her friends
are at playgroup.

267
00:11:58,466 --> 00:12:03,000
Children, today we will do drawings
for Mr. Potato.

268
00:12:03,066 --> 00:12:04,466
[children] Hooray!

269
00:12:04,533 --> 00:12:07,500
[woofs] I'm drawing a pineapple.

270
00:12:07,566 --> 00:12:09,500
I'm drawing a carrot.

271
00:12:09,566 --> 00:12:10,699
Very good.

272
00:12:10,766 --> 00:12:13,733
-What are you drawing, Emily?
-A pea.

273
00:12:13,800 --> 00:12:15,733
Lovely. And Pedro?

274
00:12:15,800 --> 00:12:18,133
It's a super potato.

275
00:12:18,199 --> 00:12:22,466
Oh, I see.
And George has drawn a wonderful tomato.

276
00:12:22,533 --> 00:12:23,600
[snorts, then giggles]

277
00:12:23,666 --> 00:12:26,500
Peppa, what vegetable have you drawn?

278
00:12:26,566 --> 00:12:30,033
[snorts] My Daddy watching television.

279
00:12:30,100 --> 00:12:31,500
[Madame Gazelle] Oh, excellent.

280
00:12:31,566 --> 00:12:37,199
Now, we put the drawings in an envelope
and post them to Mr. Potato.

281
00:12:37,266 --> 00:12:39,466
[rooster crows]

282
00:12:39,533 --> 00:12:43,300
[narrator] It is morning
and time for the Mr. Potato show.

283
00:12:43,366 --> 00:12:49,733
Please, welcome your friend
and mine, Mr. Potato.

284
00:12:49,800 --> 00:12:54,599
We posted some drawings
to Mr. Potato in an envelope.

285
00:12:54,666 --> 00:12:56,366
Did you get the envelope?

286
00:12:56,433 --> 00:13:00,566
He can't hear you, Daddy.
He's on television.

287
00:13:00,633 --> 00:13:03,166
Oh, yes, of course.

288
00:13:03,233 --> 00:13:07,300
I've received
an envelope full of drawings.

289
00:13:07,599 --> 00:13:12,699
-This tomato looks very juicy.
-That's George's picture.

290
00:13:12,766 --> 00:13:14,233
[George snorts, then giggles]

291
00:13:14,300 --> 00:13:16,033
Well done, George.

292
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:20,699
But this picture
from Peppa Pig is my favorite.

293
00:13:20,766 --> 00:13:24,099
Wow! That's my picture.

294
00:13:24,166 --> 00:13:27,099
It shows Daddy Pig watching TV.

295
00:13:27,566 --> 00:13:28,666
Hmm.

296
00:13:28,733 --> 00:13:32,433
Looks like Daddy Pig needs some exercise.

297
00:13:32,500 --> 00:13:35,166
-Eh? What?
-Come on, Daddy Pig.

298
00:13:35,233 --> 00:13:37,599
Let's do some jumping up and down.

299
00:13:38,233 --> 00:13:39,733
Oh, all right.

300
00:13:39,800 --> 00:13:41,400
[Mr. Potato] Up, down, up, down.

301
00:13:41,466 --> 00:13:43,599
[narrator] Daddy Pig
likes jumping up and down.

302
00:13:43,666 --> 00:13:45,233
[Mr. Potato] Up, down, up, down.

303
00:13:45,300 --> 00:13:47,733
[narrator] Everyone likes jumping
up and down.

304
00:13:48,800 --> 00:13:50,766
[children giggling]

305
00:13:51,000 --> 00:13:53,066
[Peppa reads on-screen text]

306
00:13:53,133 --> 00:13:56,633
[narrator] Today Peppa and her friends
are going on a train ride.

307
00:13:57,199 --> 00:13:58,666
[Mr. Rabbit blows whistle]

308
00:13:58,733 --> 00:14:00,800
[narrator] Mr. Rabbit
is the stationmaster.

309
00:14:01,033 --> 00:14:02,133
How many tickets?

310
00:14:02,199 --> 00:14:07,133
One, two, three, four, five,
six, seven, eight, nine, ten.

311
00:14:07,199 --> 00:14:10,566
Ten child tickets
and one teacher ticket, please.

312
00:14:13,133 --> 00:14:16,033
Now, children, do not lose these tickets.

313
00:14:16,699 --> 00:14:19,166
[blows whistle]
Can I see your tickets, please?

314
00:14:20,133 --> 00:14:21,300
[Pedro] Uh...

315
00:14:21,733 --> 00:14:23,699
I've lost my ticket.

316
00:14:23,766 --> 00:14:27,266
Oh, dear, Pedro, you must be more careful.

317
00:14:27,333 --> 00:14:28,500
There's your ticket.

318
00:14:28,566 --> 00:14:29,800
[giggles]

319
00:14:30,033 --> 00:14:32,800
[chuckles] Try not to lose it again.

320
00:14:33,033 --> 00:14:34,733
-[whistle toots]
-Here comes the train.

321
00:14:34,800 --> 00:14:36,233
[whistle tooting]

322
00:14:36,300 --> 00:14:37,433
Choo choo.

323
00:14:39,199 --> 00:14:41,333
[narrator] Miss Rabbit
is the train driver.

324
00:14:41,400 --> 00:14:42,500
All aboard.

325
00:14:42,566 --> 00:14:44,300
[children] Hooray!

326
00:14:45,633 --> 00:14:46,566
[blows whistle]

327
00:14:47,300 --> 00:14:48,566
[whistle tooting]

328
00:14:48,633 --> 00:14:52,666
♪ Clickety clack, clickety clack
The train rides on the track ♪

329
00:14:52,733 --> 00:14:55,766
♪ Huff and puff, huff and puff
Clickety clickety clack ♪

330
00:14:56,000 --> 00:14:56,733
[children giggle]

331
00:14:56,800 --> 00:14:59,199
Ah-ho. Here are your activity sheets.

332
00:14:59,266 --> 00:15:00,400
[children] Ooh.

333
00:15:00,466 --> 00:15:04,199
[narrator] The children have to spot
everything that is on the activity sheet.

334
00:15:04,266 --> 00:15:05,500
A boat.

335
00:15:05,566 --> 00:15:07,166
A signal box.

336
00:15:07,233 --> 00:15:08,699
[woofs] And a tunnel.

337
00:15:08,766 --> 00:15:11,699
[snorts] I can see trees.

338
00:15:11,766 --> 00:15:15,033
-Are trees on the list?
-Uh, no.

339
00:15:15,500 --> 00:15:17,633
I can see clouds.

340
00:15:17,699 --> 00:15:20,633
-[Danny] Are clouds on the list?
-No.

341
00:15:20,699 --> 00:15:23,400
I can see Granddad Dog.

342
00:15:23,466 --> 00:15:26,800
-Ahoy there.
-[all] Hello, Granddad Dog.

343
00:15:27,033 --> 00:15:28,333
[horn toots]

344
00:15:28,400 --> 00:15:29,599
[whistle toots]

345
00:15:29,666 --> 00:15:32,199
Is Granddad Dog on the list?

346
00:15:32,266 --> 00:15:33,533
Silly Peppa.

347
00:15:33,599 --> 00:15:36,366
My Granddad won't be on the list.

348
00:15:36,433 --> 00:15:38,566
But he is sailing a boat.

349
00:15:38,633 --> 00:15:41,233
And a boat is on the list.

350
00:15:41,300 --> 00:15:42,266
[children] Hooray!

351
00:15:42,333 --> 00:15:45,466
[narrator] The children tick the boat
on their activity sheets.

352
00:15:45,533 --> 00:15:46,666
[blows whistle]

353
00:15:46,733 --> 00:15:48,033
Tickets, please.

354
00:15:48,099 --> 00:15:51,266
[narrator] Mr. Rabbit has come
to check everyone's ticket.

355
00:15:53,166 --> 00:15:56,000
Uh... I think I've lost my ticket.

356
00:15:56,066 --> 00:15:57,733
Oh, dear. Oh, dear.

357
00:15:57,800 --> 00:16:00,500
[meows] There's your ticket, Pedro.

358
00:16:00,566 --> 00:16:02,733
-You were sitting on it.
-[giggles]

359
00:16:02,800 --> 00:16:05,666
Now, you try not to lose it again, Pedro.

360
00:16:06,800 --> 00:16:09,466
[narrator] The train is going
slowly uphill.

361
00:16:13,099 --> 00:16:14,166
[children] Whee!

362
00:16:14,233 --> 00:16:16,366
[narrator] The train is going
quickly downhill.

363
00:16:16,433 --> 00:16:17,699
[children giggling]

364
00:16:17,766 --> 00:16:20,766
Madame Gazelle, I feel a bit sick.

365
00:16:21,000 --> 00:16:23,266
Can I go to the front, please?

366
00:16:23,333 --> 00:16:26,666
Okay, Pedro.
You can go to the front of the train.

367
00:16:26,733 --> 00:16:28,033
[Pedro giggles]

368
00:16:28,099 --> 00:16:31,300
♪ Doo da dum dum, da dee da ♪

369
00:16:31,366 --> 00:16:33,699
-[neighs]
-Hello, Pedro.

370
00:16:33,766 --> 00:16:38,099
Not feeling very well? Would you
like to drive the train for a bit?

371
00:16:38,566 --> 00:16:39,800
Yes, please.

372
00:16:40,033 --> 00:16:41,300
[Pedro giggling]

373
00:16:41,366 --> 00:16:42,766
[whistle toots]

374
00:16:44,400 --> 00:16:48,000
♪ Clickety clack, clickety clack
The train rides on the track ♪

375
00:16:48,066 --> 00:16:51,533
♪ Huff and puff, huff and puff
The train rides on the track ♪

376
00:16:51,599 --> 00:16:52,633
[whistle toots]

377
00:16:52,699 --> 00:16:54,266
[children giggling]

378
00:16:55,266 --> 00:16:58,000
[bell clanging]

379
00:16:58,066 --> 00:17:02,000
[snorts] A signal box. That's on our list.

380
00:17:02,066 --> 00:17:03,366
[children] Hooray!

381
00:17:03,433 --> 00:17:07,066
[narrator] The children tick
the signal box on their activity sheets.

382
00:17:07,533 --> 00:17:11,700
The signal has stopped the train
so that someone important can cross.

383
00:17:12,633 --> 00:17:14,000
[quacking]

384
00:17:15,566 --> 00:17:17,599
It's Mrs. Duck and her friends.

385
00:17:17,666 --> 00:17:19,333
[all quacking]

386
00:17:25,399 --> 00:17:28,466
Oh, we still haven't seen a tunnel.

387
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:29,800
[all gasp]

388
00:17:30,033 --> 00:17:32,166
[Peppa] Oh, it's gone dark.

389
00:17:32,233 --> 00:17:35,033
-[Suzy] We're in a tunnel.
-[all giggle]

390
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:38,533
[narrator] The tunnel is the last thing
on the activity sheet.

391
00:17:38,600 --> 00:17:40,166
[all] Hooray! [giggle]

392
00:17:42,666 --> 00:17:44,433
Last stop.

393
00:17:44,500 --> 00:17:46,166
All change.

394
00:17:46,233 --> 00:17:48,000
Everybody off now.

395
00:17:49,000 --> 00:17:52,399
But, Madame Gazelle,
how are we going to get home?

396
00:17:52,466 --> 00:17:55,399
[chuckles] Peppa, we are back
where we started.

397
00:17:55,466 --> 00:17:58,500
[narrator] The train has gone
in a big circle.

398
00:17:58,566 --> 00:18:00,500
[blows whistle] Tickets, please.

399
00:18:00,566 --> 00:18:02,166
[children giggle]

400
00:18:02,233 --> 00:18:03,233
Um...

401
00:18:03,300 --> 00:18:05,600
Pedro's lost his ticket again.

402
00:18:05,666 --> 00:18:07,766
-Um...
-Pedro.

403
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,399
Can I have my hat back, please?

404
00:18:10,466 --> 00:18:12,800
[children] There's Pedro's ticket.

405
00:18:13,033 --> 00:18:15,600
Oh, that's where I put it.

406
00:18:15,666 --> 00:18:17,666
[all laughing]

407
00:18:18,800 --> 00:18:22,300
♪ Clickety clack, clickety clack
The train rides on the track ♪

408
00:18:22,366 --> 00:18:26,233
♪ Huff and puff, huff and puff
Clickety clickety clack ♪

409
00:18:26,300 --> 00:18:29,766
♪ Clickety clack, clickety clack
The train rides on the track ♪

410
00:18:30,000 --> 00:18:33,266
♪ Huff and puff, huff and puff
The train rides on the track ♪

411
00:18:33,333 --> 00:18:34,300
[whistle toots]

